  "description": "#4016 implemented the spec QphDS@Size metric and its execution order (TPC-DS 4.0.0 clause 7.4.2), exporting it only when every input is valid. It was verified by unit tests with stubbed phases; the full sequence was not run on a platform. Maintenance now refuses to run on DuckDB, PostgreSQL and SQLite when a target table has an enforced primary key (owner decision on the dsdgen key overlap), so the run must use notuning or non-enforced keys.\n\nChange. Run the full official TPC-DS sequence on DuckDB at SF1 with --tuning notuning. Confirm QphDS@Size is computed and exported, that each input (T_PT, T_TT1, T_TT2, T_DM1, T_DM2, T_LD) is present and comes from the right phase, and that the withholding rules trigger when an input is invalid. Fix any defect found.\n\nGuardrails: work in a linked worktree (make worktree-create); never edit the primary clone; heavy work only through make heavy-run; container checks under mocker one stack at a time (limits in tests/uat docs and the uat-mocker-compose-gaps-20261106 context); no live cloud without owner approval; no explanatory comments; changelog fragment if user-facing.",
